class.description:
[b]Levels[/b]
A level is spawned like any other node, with [method configure_scene] in its root. A player receives the level while one of their [member NetwPlayer.entities] is in it, so spawn players into it with [method spawn_player], here and in the [method configure_join] handler. [NetwScene] covers the rest.
[codeblock]
# arena.gd
func _init() -> void:
    Netw.configure_scene(self)

# game.gd
func _init() -> void:
    Netw.configure_spawn(make_arena)
    Netw.configure_spawn(make_car)

func make_arena() -> Node:
    return preload("res://arena.tscn").instantiate()

func make_car() -> Node:
    return preload("res://car.tscn").instantiate()

func start_match(lobby: Node) -> void:
    Netw.despawn(lobby)
    var arena: Node = Netw.spawn(make_arena)
    add_child(arena)
    for player: NetwPlayer in Netw.session(self).players:
        arena.add_child(Netw.spawn_player(player, make_car))
[/codeblock]

method.description:
[codeblock]
func _init() -> void:
    Netw.configure_database(self, &"saves") \
            .backend(preload("res://save_backend.tres"))

func _ready() -> void:
    var db: NetwDatabase = Netw.session(self).database(&"saves")
    var error: Error = await db.open(&"campaign").wait()
[/codeblock]
Reach the [NetwDatabase] through [method NetwSession.database].

[param callable] must name a script method. Anonymous callbacks are refused.
[codeblock]
func _init() -> void:
    Netw.configure_rpc(self.aim).controller().quantize(
            NetwQuantizeAngle.new().bits(12).centered(),
    )

@rpc("any_peer", "unreliable")
func aim(yaw: float) -> void:
    turret.rotation.y = yaw
[/codeblock]

[codeblock]
func _init() -> void:
    Netw.configure_spawn(make_bullet)

func make_bullet(direction: Vector2) -> Node:
    var bullet := BulletScene.instantiate()
    bullet.direction = direction
    return bullet

func fire(direction: Vector2) -> void:
    muzzle.add_child(Netw.spawn(make_bullet, direction))
[/codeblock]
The [Callable] must be configured before [method spawn] or [method spawn_async] uses it. It may await only under [method spawn_async].

Picks which [NetwEntity] instances outlive a server transfer in [constant NetwSession.TRANSFER_REJOIN]. The new server calls [param keep] with the root node of each [NetwEntity] it took over, and despawns the ones it answers [code]false[/code] for before any client gets the world again.
[codeblock]
func _init() -> void:
    Netw.configure_transfer(keeps)

func keeps(node: Node) -> bool:
    return not node.is_in_group(&"loot")
[/codeblock]
Declare it on every peer, since any of them can become the server.

Calls [param callable] on the server and returns a [NetwPromise] with its return value.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
func buy_shield() -> void:
    var sold: bool = await Netw.request(shop.buy, &"shield").wait()

@rpc("any_peer")
func buy(item: StringName) -> bool:
    return await stock.take(item)
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
public async void BuyShield()
{
    bool sold = (await Netw.Request(shop, MethodName.Buy, "shield")).AsBool();
}

[Rpc(MultiplayerApi.RpcMode.AnyPeer)]
public Variant Buy(StringName item) => NetwPromise.FromTask(stock.Take(item));
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
The method must be an RPC, as for [method rpc]. The promise fails at once when the node is not part of a spawned [NetwEntity].
The method may [code]await[/code], and the reply is sent when it returns. A method whose node is freed while it waits never replies, so the promise fails when it times out.

Calls [param callable] on every peer that can see the node, and returns a [NetwGroupPromise] with each return value. The promise fails at once when the node is not part of a spawned [NetwEntity].
A method declared with [method NetwMemberConfig.call_local] or a [code]call_local[/code] [annotation @GDScript.@rpc] also runs on this peer, and its value joins [member NetwGroupPromise.results] under this peer's id. Otherwise this peer is not asked. The method may [code]await[/code], as for [method request]. A method that takes longer than 5 seconds declares its own deadline with [method NetwMemberConfig.timeout].
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
extends Node

const MATCH := "res://match.tscn"

var warm: PackedScene

func _init() -> void:
    Netw.configure_entity(self)
    Netw.configure_rpc(preload_level).timeout(60.0)
    Netw.configure_spawn(make_match)
    Netw.configure_spawn(make_player)

func start_match() -> void:
    var loads := Netw.request_all(preload_level, MATCH)
    await loads.wait()
    if loads.is_failed or false in loads.results.values():
        return
    var arena: Node = Netw.spawn(make_match)
    add_child(arena)
    for player: NetwPlayer in Netw.session(self).players:
        arena.add_child(Netw.spawn_player(player, make_player))

func make_match() -> Node:
    return warm.instantiate()

@rpc("authority")
func preload_level(path: String) -> bool:
    ResourceLoader.load_threaded_request(path)
    while ResourceLoader.load_threaded_get_status(path) \
            == ResourceLoader.THREAD_LOAD_IN_PROGRESS:
        await get_tree().process_frame
    warm = ResourceLoader.load_threaded_get(path)
    return warm != null
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
public partial class SceneManager : Node
{
    const string Match = "res://match.tscn";

    PackedScene warm;

    public SceneManager()
    {
        Netw.ConfigureEntity(this);
        Netw.ConfigureRpc(this, MethodName.PreloadLevel).Timeout(60.0);
        Netw.ConfigureSpawn(this, MethodName.MakeMatch);
        Netw.ConfigureSpawn(this, MethodName.MakePlayer);
    }

    public async void StartMatch()
    {
        NetwGroupPromise loads = await Netw.RequestAll(this, MethodName.PreloadLevel, Match);
        if (loads.IsFailed || loads.Results.Values.Any(loaded => !loaded.AsBool()))
            return;
        Node arena = Netw.Spawn(this, MethodName.MakeMatch);
        AddChild(arena);
        foreach (NetwPlayer player in Netw.Session(this).Players)
            arena.AddChild(Netw.SpawnPlayer(player, this, MethodName.MakePlayer));
    }

    public Node MakeMatch() => warm.Instantiate();

    public Variant PreloadLevel(string path) => NetwPromise.FromTask(Preload(path));

    async Task<bool> Preload(string path)
    {
        ResourceLoader.LoadThreadedRequest(path);
        while (ResourceLoader.LoadThreadedGetStatus(path)
                == ResourceLoader.ThreadLoadStatus.InProgress)
            await ToSignal(GetTree(), SceneTree.SignalName.ProcessFrame);
        warm = ResourceLoader.LoadThreadedGet(path) as PackedScene;
        return warm != null;
    }
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]

Moves every entity in [param entities] back to [param tick], calls [param body], moves them back, and returns what [param body] returned. Apply what the query found after it returns.
[codeblock]
func _fire(ctx: NetwActionContext, origin: Vector3, aim: Vector3) -> void:
    var targets := players.entities.keys()
    targets.erase(entity)
    var hit: Dictionary = Netw.rewind(targets, ctx.view_tick, func() -> Dictionary:
        var ray := PhysicsRayQueryParameters3D.create(
                origin, origin + aim * RANGE, HITBOX_LAYER)
        ray.collide_with_areas = true
        return get_world_3d().direct_space_state.intersect_ray(ray))
    if hit:
        (hit.collider.owner as Player).health -= DAMAGE
[/codeblock]
Here [code]players[/code] is a [NetwInterestLayer], the set of entities a shot can hit.

Returns a copy of the state of [param entity] at [param tick]. It is empty when nothing was recorded. A property declared on a child node is keyed by its path, such as [code]&"Hurtbox:offset"[/code].
[codeblock]
func _place_bomb(ctx: NetwActionContext, pos: Vector2) -> void:
    var past := Netw.sample(entity, ctx.view_tick)
    if not past.has_value(&"position"):
        ctx.deny()
        return
[/codeblock]

Returns the multiplayer scene [param node] is in, or [code]null[/code] when no scene was found. Use [method NetwSession.find_scene] to find one by name.
[codeblock]
var here := Netw.scene(self)
var track := Netw.session(self).find_scene(&"Track")
[/codeblock]

Like [method spawn], and [param fn] may await. The [NetwPromise] settles with the node once [param fn] returns on this peer. Add the node before the next tick.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
func start(path: String) -> void:
    var level: Node = await Netw.spawn_async(make_level, path).wait()
    add_child(level)

func make_level(path: String) -> Node:
    loading_screen.show()
    ResourceLoader.load_threaded_request(path)
    while ResourceLoader.load_threaded_get_status(path) \
            == ResourceLoader.THREAD_LOAD_IN_PROGRESS:
        await get_tree().process_frame
    loading_screen.hide()
    return ResourceLoader.load_threaded_get(path).instantiate()
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
public async void Start(string path)
{
    Node level = await Netw.SpawnAsync(this, MethodName.MakeLevel, path).AsTask(v => v.As<Node>());
    AddChild(level);
}

public Variant MakeLevel(string path) => NetwPromise.FromTask(LoadLevel(path));

async Task<Node> LoadLevel(string path)
{
    loadingScreen.Show();
    ResourceLoader.LoadThreadedRequest(path);
    while (ResourceLoader.LoadThreadedGetStatus(path)
            == ResourceLoader.ThreadLoadStatus.InProgress)
        await ToSignal(GetTree(), SceneTree.SignalName.ProcessFrame);
    loadingScreen.Hide();
    return (ResourceLoader.LoadThreadedGet(path) as PackedScene).Instantiate();
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
Every peer builds its own copy at its own pace. On a client, nodes spawned into it and RPCs sent to it wait until that client's copy is built. The promise says nothing about clients, and [method request_all] shows how to wait until every peer has loaded a level before you spawn it.
[b]Server Only.[/b]
